Good morning Mr. White,

Thank you for reaching out to our office regarding this situation with OPRD=
. In terms of how the process works regarding audit requests, those request=
s go through the Secretary of State's Audit Division, and they determine if=
 there is an adequate basis in order to conduct an audit based on a state a=
gency's "waste, inefficiency or abuse of government resources."

You can submit that request here: Report Waste, Inefficiency, or Abuse of S=
tate Government Resources | Oregon Secretary of State | State of Oregon<htt=
ps://sos.oregon.gov/audits/Pages/accountability.aspx>

If the SOS's office determines that there is a basis for an audit, then the=
 audit is set to begin based on the ability of the office to conduct it, an=
d it is calendared and the process can take 1-2 years.

At that point, the Joint Legislative Audit Committee (JLAC) reviews audits =
from the SOS's Division of Audits, and the committee is responsible for sel=
ecting audit reports for review and recommending changes or remediation.

Thank you again for reaching out to us.

Sincerely,

Jon Pugsley
Legislative Director

