<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Good morning Mr. White, <o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Thank you for reaching out to our office regarding t=
his situation with OPRD. In terms of how the process works regarding audit =
requests, those requests go through the Secretary of State&#8217;s Audit Di=
vision, and they determine if there is an
 adequate basis in order to conduct an audit based on a state agency&#8217;=
s &#8220;waste, inefficiency or abuse of government resources.&#8221;
<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">You can submit that request here: <a href=3D"https:/=
/sos.oregon.gov/audits/Pages/accountability.aspx">
Report Waste, Inefficiency, or Abuse of State Government Resources | Oregon=
 Secretary of State | State of Oregon</a><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">If the SOS&#8217;s office determines that there is a=
 basis for an audit, then the audit is set to begin based on the ability of=
 the office to conduct it, and it is calendared and the process can take 1-=
2 years.
<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">At that point, the Joint Legislative Audit Committee=
 (JLAC) reviews audits from the SOS&#8217;s Division of Audits, and the com=
mittee is responsible for selecting audit reports for review and recommendi=
ng changes or remediation.
<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Thank you again for reaching out to us. <o:p></o:p><=
/p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Sincerely, <o:p></o:p></p>
